<Styles xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml">

    <!-- The form controls whose colours are NOT reachable through a resource key
         - see docs/LunaP.md §48 and Theme/FluentBridge.axaml for the ones that
         are.

         Theme/FluentBridge.axaml does almost all of this work by handing LunaP's
         colours to FluentTheme's own keys, which leaves every template alone.
         A handful of controls do not read a key at all: their ControlTheme sets
         Foreground and Background on the control itself, so the only way to
         reach them is a Setter of our own.

         THESE ARE STYLES AND NOT TEMPLATES, which is the whole of §48's method.
         A Setter changes a value Fluent's template then uses; replacing the
         template would mean owning Fluent's keyboard handling, its focus
         adorners and its accessibility behaviour forever, for a colour. -->

    <!-- ProgressBar names no resource for either half of itself: the filled part
         is its Foreground and the track is its Background, both set by Fluent's
         ControlTheme directly.

         MeterRow is unaffected and that is worth knowing before anybody
         "simplifies" this away. Its bar takes a colour from the load ramp in
         code (§2.2), and a local value beats a style, so the ramp still wins
         where it is set and this only reaches bars nobody has coloured. -->
    <Style Selector="ProgressBar">
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource LunaAccent}" />
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource LunaBorder}" />
    </Style>

</Styles>
